# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
#
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
#
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD frame-1 64179 lightbluishgray
ADD pin-1 6562 lightbluishgray
ADD pin-2 6562 lightbluishgray
ADD pin-3 6562 lightbluishgray
ADD pin-4 6562 lightbluishgray
CONNECT pin-1.? -> frame-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-2.? -> frame-1.hole5~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-3.? -> frame-1.hole16~ STIFF
CONNECT pin-4.? -> frame-1.hole20~ STIFF
WHY Starts the build with the 7x5 open frame and presses a pin joiner into each of its four corner holes, giving the next parts posts to sit on.

STEP 2
ADD beam-1 32523 red
ADD beam-2 32523 red
CONNECT beam-1.hole1 -> pin-1.? STIFF
CONNECT beam-2.hole1 -> pin-3.? STIFF
WHY Presses the two red 1x3 beams onto the free ends of two corner pins, starting the inner cage that will hold the gear cluster.

STEP 3
ADD fric-1 2780 black
ADD fric-2 2780 black
CONNECT fric-1.pin1 -> frame-1.hole10~ STIFF
CONNECT fric-1.pin2 -> beam-1.hole3 STIFF
CONNECT fric-2.pin1 -> frame-1.hole11~ STIFF
CONNECT fric-2.pin2 -> beam-2.hole3 STIFF
WHY Pins the free ends of the two red beams into the frame's middle holes with friction pins, squaring up the cage.

STEP 4
ADD bevel-1 6589 tan
ADD bevel-2 6589 tan
WHY Drops the two 12-tooth bevel gears into the cage; they will lock onto the differential housings' stubs once those are built.

STEP 5
ADD gear20-1 24201 black
ADD gear20-2 24201 black
WHY Adds the two 20-tooth gears that will carry the housings' output drive once the housings are built.

STEP 6
ADD beam7-1 32524 lightbluishgray
ADD beam7-2 32524 lightbluishgray
CONNECT beam7-1.hole1 -> pin-2.? STIFF
CONNECT beam7-2.hole1 -> pin-4.? STIFF
WHY Presses the two long 1x7 beams onto the remaining corner pins, extending the frame into the side rails that will carry the output axles.

STEP 7
GROUP arm-a
ADD housing-a 60c01 black
ADD axlecon-a1 32184 black
ADD axlecon-a2 32184 black
ADD cross-a1 32184 black
ADD cross-a2 32184 black
ADD elbow-a1 32014 red
ADD elbow-a2 32014 red
ADD cap-a 18654 lightbluishgray
CONNECT axlecon-a1.? -> housing-a.stub1? LOCKED
CONNECT axlecon-a2.? -> housing-a.stub2? LOCKED
CONNECT cross-a1.? -> housing-a.stub3? LOCKED
CONNECT cross-a2.? -> housing-a.stub4? LOCKED
CONNECT elbow-a1.axlehole1 -> housing-a.stub5? LOCKED
CONNECT elbow-a2.axlehole1 -> housing-a.stub6? LOCKED
CONNECT cap-a.hole1 -> housing-a.hub1? TURNS
CONNECT bevel-1.axlehole1 -> housing-a.stub7? LOCKED
CONNECT gear20-1.? -> housing-a.stub8? LOCKED
END
ATTACH arm-a
CONNECT axlecon-a1.? -> beam-1.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Builds the first differential housing with its red angled spokes, cross connectors and cap, locks the 12- and 20-tooth gears onto its stubs, and attaches the finished arm to the cage.

STEP 8
GROUP arm-b
ADD housing-b 60c01 black
ADD axlecon-b1 32184 black
ADD axlecon-b2 32184 black
ADD cross-b1 32184 black
ADD cross-b2 32184 black
ADD elbow-b1 32014 red
ADD elbow-b2 32014 red
ADD cap-b 18654 lightbluishgray
CONNECT axlecon-b1.? -> housing-b.stub1? LOCKED
CONNECT axlecon-b2.? -> housing-b.stub2? LOCKED
CONNECT cross-b1.? -> housing-b.stub3? LOCKED
CONNECT cross-b2.? -> housing-b.stub4? LOCKED
CONNECT elbow-b1.axlehole1 -> housing-b.stub5? LOCKED
CONNECT elbow-b2.axlehole1 -> housing-b.stub6? LOCKED
CONNECT cap-b.hole1 -> housing-b.hub1? TURNS
CONNECT bevel-2.axlehole1 -> housing-b.stub7? LOCKED
CONNECT gear20-2.? -> housing-b.stub8? LOCKED
END
ATTACH arm-b
CONNECT axlecon-b1.? -> beam-2.hole2~ STIFF
WHY Builds the mirrored second differential housing the same way and attaches it to the opposite side of the cage, completing both gear clusters.

STEP 9
ADD lock-1 6587 lightbluishgray
ADD lock-2 6587 lightbluishgray
ADD lock-3 6587 lightbluishgray
ADD lock-4 6587 lightbluishgray
CONNECT lock-1.axle1 -> housing-a.stub9? LOCKED
CONNECT lock-1.pin1 -> beam7-1.hole4~ TURNS
CONNECT lock-2.axle1 -> housing-a.stub10? LOCKED
CONNECT lock-2.pin1 -> beam7-1.hole2~ TURNS
CONNECT lock-3.axle1 -> housing-b.stub9? LOCKED
CONNECT lock-3.pin1 -> beam7-2.hole4~ TURNS
CONNECT lock-4.axle1 -> housing-b.stub10? LOCKED
CONNECT lock-4.pin1 -> beam7-2.hole2~ TURNS
WHY Locks the four stud-capped axle pins through both housings' last stubs and out into the side rails, bracing the gear clusters and finishing the differential.
